# The output contract of `execute_graph.rs` / `sink.rs`: two shapes, and one
# predicate whose range is a SHAPE rather than a literal.
#
# `ex:placedBy @ex:Person` is what makes `placedBy` an EDGE. Nothing else can:
# the template-skeleton guess that used to infer one (`fossil-mir`'s
# `subject_skeletons`) is deleted, so an accept-all descriptor now yields a
# string column named `placedBy` and no edge table at all.
#
# The values are deliberately un-narrowed (`.`) everywhere else: the columns
# these tests assert on are typed by the MIR (String, absent an input schema on
# the source), and a datatype here would only add a second opinion.
PREFIX ex: <https://example.org/>

ex:Person {
  ex:name .
}

ex:Order {
  ex:placedBy @ex:Person ;
  ex:total .
}
